Title: THE WINTER DISPATCH
Author: Claire Montgomery
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. RESISTANCE SAFE HOUSE - LYON - NIGHT - 1943

Candlelight. MARIE DUBOIS, 30s, presses a SEALED ENVELOPE flat under a floorboard. Her brother LUC, 20s, watches the street.
MARIE
The courier comes at dawn. Until then, no one opens the door.

INT. GERMAN FIELD OFFICE - DAY

HAUPTMANN STRASSER reviews a sketch of Marie. A sergeant sets down a confiscated BICYCLE with a bent front wheel.
STRASSER
She passes messages through the market on Rue Victor Hugo.

EXT. LYON MARKET - MORNING

Marie sells herbs from a stall. ANTOINE, 50s, baker, buys thyme and slides a note into her basket.
ANTOINE
They searched the canal house yesterday. Be careful.

INT. RESISTANCE SAFE HOUSE - NIGHT

Luc returns mud-spattered. Marie reads Antoine's note by candle — STRASSER KNOWS THE ROUTE.
LUC
We move the envelope tonight. I know another path.

EXT. CANAL PATH - NIGHT

Marie and Luc pedal through fog on the repaired bicycle. Headlights appear behind them. Marie clutches the SEALED ENVELOPE inside her coat.
MARIE
If they stop us, you run. The names cannot die with us.

FADE OUT.


THE END
